WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.440
KrishiNexus OS. Built by Team Heat Wave,
Tanvir Hossin, team lead.

2
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.920
Md. Omar Faruk, AI and machine learning
engineer.

3
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.480
Md. Abdur Rahman, full-stack and backend.

4
00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:14.240
Mohammed Mahmud Parvez, full-stack
developer.

5
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.680
Md. Morsalin, full-stack and backend.

6
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:21.600
And our advisor, Md Rifat, domain and
network expert, joining us online.

7
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.640
In Bangladesh, a potato farmer often sells
below cost.

8
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:29.440
Between the field and the buyer, five
tiers of middlemen can mark the price up

9
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.080
by as much as 116%.

10
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.320
Traders hold 77% of the cold storage
space.

11
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.800
And a single flash flood can wipe out an
entire season.

12
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.560
KrishiNexus OS is one AI operating system
for everyone in that chain.

13
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:48.680
The farmer, the co-op, the cold store, the
buyer, the truck driver and the bank.

14
00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:51.280
Each one signs in to their own workspace.

15
00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.560
Rahim is a potato farmer in Rangpur.

16
00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:55.680
He simply asks in his own dialect.

17
00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.440
After he gives consent, four AI agents
grade his crop,

18
00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:02.560
compare today's market with cold storage
and a shared truck,

19
00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.080
and check the flood risk.

20
00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.160
A circuit breaker stops him from selling
below his cost,

21
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:08.800
and it shows its working.

22
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.800
He can also photograph his potatoes.

23
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:14.160
A trained vision model finds every tuber
and its defects,

24
00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.080
then signs a quality certificate.

25
00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:19.280
Buyers and banks can verify that
certificate for themselves.

26
00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:22.440
Behind every answer, you can watch the
agents work.

27
00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:24.360
They retrieve Bangladeshi farm data,

28
00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:26.920
call live tools through three MCP servers,

29
00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.720
and every step is traced.

30
00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:31.840
It even runs offline on a fine-tuned
Bangla model

31
00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:33.040
at a village kiosk.

32
00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:36.520
Co-ops pool small harvests into full five-
ton trucks.

33
00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:39.640
The cold store sees live chamber sensors
in a 3D twin,

34
00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:41.840
and when a flood or heat alert arrives,

35
00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.280
the trucks are rerouted.

36
00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:45.160
Rahim can also sell directly.

37
00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:47.840
He lists his lot, traders bid in the open,

38
00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.440
and he accepts the best bid.

39
00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.160
The payment is held in escrow.

40
00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.440
A driver takes the job

41
00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.760
and reports the load temperature along the
road.

42
00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:57.920
Our shelf life model checks that the
potatoes will arrive safe,

43
00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:00.920
and on delivery, the payment is released
to Rahim.

44
00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:04.600
Banks see a credit score from 300 to 850.

45
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.400
It is backed by satellite flood checks

46
00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.760
and signed certificates.

47
00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.640
So, a farmer without collateral

48
00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:11.040
can still get credit.

49
00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:12.640
We trained five models,

50
00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.320
and we publish every score,

51
00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.520
including the ones that miss their
targets.

52
00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:18.120
The app asks for consent.

53
00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.000
It removes names and phone numbers.

54
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.160
It keeps data for 24 hours only,

55
00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.560
and it always leaves the final decision to
the farmer.

56
00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:29.600
KrishiNexus also fits in a farmer's
pocket.

57
00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:31.320
Our Android app speaks Bangla.

58
00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.600
Rahim asks out loud,

59
00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:34.080
and hears the answer back.

60
00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.680
He photographs his harvest,

61
00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.920
and gets a signed grade in seconds.

62
00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:39.520
Buyers bid from their phones,

63
00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:41.200
drivers share their live location,

64
00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.160
and everyone follows the sale in real
time.

65
00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.360
One pooled truck covers its costs.

66
00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.960
A district breaks even at 16 trucks a
month.

67
00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.800
We start a field test this December,

68
00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.680
and a potato pilot in January.

69
00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.680
This is KrishiNexus OS by Team Heat Wave.

70
00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.680
Try it now at tanvir.health.
